From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pmaports <pmaports@localhost>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 10:52:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bus: mhi: host: serve a flashless SDX55M's Sahara and EFS
 channels

A flashless SDX55M (Xiaomi Mi 10) gets only SBL over BHI. SBL then asks
for every other image over Sahara on channel 2/3, and in mission mode the
modem syncs its NV file system to the host over channel 10/11 (Sahara
memory debug). Give the generic SDX55 entry those channels, and add a
small MHI client driver that exposes them as /dev/mhi_sahara and
/dev/mhi_efs for a userspace server.

The Mi 10's modem reports subsystem 17cb:010c, like the Foxconn T99W175,
so a module parameter (sdx55_flashless) tells the driver which one it is.

write() sends its buffer as one transfer of chained TREs, because SBL
consumes a READ_DATA answer only once it sees the end of the transfer.
read() returns at most one transfer.
